{
  "mn110:0.1": "Middle Discourses 110 ",
  "mn110:0.2": "The Shorter Discourse on the Full-Moon Night ",
  "mn110:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn110:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery. ",
  "mn110:2.1": "Now, at that time it was the sabbath—the full moon on the fifteenth day—and the Buddha was sitting in the open surrounded by the Saṅgha of monks. ",
  "mn110:2.2": "Then the Buddha looked around the Saṅgha of monks, who were so very silent. He addressed them, ",
  "mn110:3.1": "“Monks, could an untrue person know of an untrue person: ",
  "mn110:3.2": "‘This worthy one is an untrue person’?” ",
  "mn110:3.3": "“No, sir.” ",
  "mn110:3.4": "“Good, monks! ",
  "mn110:3.5": "It’s impossible, it can’t happen, that an untrue person could know of an untrue person: ",
  "mn110:3.6": "‘This worthy one is an untrue person.’ ",
  "mn110:3.7": "But could an untrue person know of a true person: ",
  "mn110:3.8": "‘This worthy one is a true person’?” ",
  "mn110:3.9": "“No, sir.” ",
  "mn110:3.10": "“Good, monks! ",
  "mn110:3.11": "That too is impossible. ",
  "mn110:3.12": "",
  "mn110:4.1": "An untrue person has bad qualities, is devoted to untrue persons, and has the intentions, counsel, speech, actions, views, and giving of an untrue person. ",
  "mn110:5.1": "And how does an untrue person have bad qualities? ",
  "mn110:5.2": "It’s when an untrue person is faithless, shameless, im